  "note": "Independent hermitage_theatre/Q2349693 member of the five-building main Hermitage complex. Named native theatre parent52776559217972/relation1084724 and the co-located Peter the Great Winter Palace museum POI identify this physical theatre block; the latter does not require a duplicate building asset. Native outline approximately72.9x47.3m includes one12x13m courtyard. Rear block52776559217973 is separately named/typed by the map and remains independent, as does covered gallery52776566225543 owned by Old Hermitage. +X internal runs along the river facade away from Winter Canal, -Z faces Neva, world heading0/native east-south/internal main-site axis0.630352782657rad. Anchor[30.3179794549942,59.94263555424804]. Two ordinary exterior photographs actually viewed establish engaged columns, window/transom/niche rhythm, palette and rounded upper canal corner. A common ground sample at the mapped south plaza aligns all five building floors. Molen’s bounded Hermitage waterfront grade is 17.50 m and blends into the retained Terrarium field. Source building outlines, courtyard openings and independent roads are preserved. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
